{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0857"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c072): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c072.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0857"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/football","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__football.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",1046],["+","Winning at home has a tradition of its own. The very first champion was also the first host to lift the trophy: Uruguay beat Argentina 4–2 in Montevideo on 30 July 1930. Italy repeated the feat in 1934, England in 1966, West Germany in 1974, Argentina in 1978 and France in 1998, so the Germans of 1974 were already the fourth home winners, not the first.\n\n"],["=",55]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",1014],["+","Der Heimsieg hat eine eigene Tradition. Schon der allererste Weltmeister war auch der erste Gastgeber, der den Pokal gewann: Uruguay schlug Argentinien am 30. Juli 1930 in Montevideo mit 4:2. Italien wiederholte das Kunststück 1934, England 1966, die Bundesrepublik 1974, Argentinien 1978 und Frankreich 1998 – die Deutschen von 1974 waren also bereits die vierten Heimweltmeister, nicht die ersten.\n\n"],["=",45]]},{"field":"notesEn","old":"","new":"The card claimed West Germany (1974) was the first world champion to win at home; Uruguay (1930), Italy (1934) and England (1966) had all done so before."},{"field":"notesDe","old":"","new":"Die Karte behauptete, die Bundesrepublik sei 1974 der erste Weltmeister im eigenen Land gewesen; Uruguay (1930), Italien (1934) und England (1966) hatten das schon vorher geschafft."}]},
